From cae4b4464c289eb3d57a01c3361f810f7d603ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:02:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Rebuild visit logging as full check-in/check-out with
 photo evidence

Replaces the single-tap visit log with a real field-verification flow:
check-in requires GPS within 100m of the dealer (hard block) plus a
mandatory duty-on photo; check-out requires shop board, shop interior,
and dealer visiting-card photos plus a short shop-interior video, all
geo-tagged via a canvas overlay burned onto the image. A dealer's
first-ever check-in sets its saved location if it has none yet. A rep
can only have one open visit at a time, enforced both in the RPC and
via a partial unique index.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
